<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abu'l-Fath Muhammad ibn Annaz</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 990–1010</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Muhammad ibn Annaz</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abu'l-Fath Muhammad ibn Annaz was a Kurdish chief of the Shadhanjan tribe who founded the Annazid dynasty. Around 990, as Buyid authority weakened, he established himself at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hulwan">Hulwan</a> on the road from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamadan">Hamadan</a>, and he ruled the frontier lands of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> and eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> for about twenty years. His descendants held parts of the region until the Seljuk period.</p></div>
